==Appearance==
<tabber>
|-|Default=
Blot is a slate gray ink blob. His head is teardrop shaped and has parts of it dripping down the left side of his face and the right side of his head, giving it a hair-like appearance. He also has light shines shaped as bubble-like, upside-down exclamation marks on both ends of his hair and a longer one on top of his head, making him appear glossy. The ink also drips around his neck. He wears mime makeup around his singular right eye, along with triangular marks above and below the eye, and his cheeks are a darker shade of gray. He also has no visible mouth. He wears a black and white striped shirt and white gloves with two light gray stitches. His legs gradually darken with a slightly darker wavy layer below the knees and an even darker one below for his feet which seem to melt into the ground, being cone shaped and leaving an ink trail. When attacked, he has a forlorn face.
|-|Vintage=
Vintage Blot is now purely gray without any subtle blue hues and has an additional layer of gradually darkening ink in between the second and third. His shirt is also now black with white stripes and his gloves black with white stitches. His singular eye is also pie-cut to the right.
|-|Show-Time=
[[Show-Time Cosmetic Pack|Show-Time]] Blot is dark cyan with legs that darken into a midnight blue, while the tip behind his head is slightly longer with a similar pattern to his feet. He has white face paint with teal makeup around his eye and additional dark blue paint marks, specifically an upside-down arch above his eye resembling an eyebrow and a teardrop below. His shirt has also been recolored cream yellow with light orange stripes and his gloves have red stitching. He wears a bright red beret with a loop pattern colored the same light yellow and a darker red lower half and tail. He now wears shorts that sport a similar pattern, but they are primarily maroon with the lighter red below the loops. Instead of ink on his neck, there is a red bandana with two short tails that have darker tips and a soft yellow stripe separates it from the rest of the bandana. Similarly, he wears a satchel with a dark red handle that hangs on his right shoulder while the other components, consisting of a dark flap, red body, and a deep cyan droplet in a gold frame that seals the satchel, rest under his left arm. His inky trail is also now the thick, blue shade used for his feet. He has an additional orange and blue gradient trail of tickets labeled "TICKET," circus tents, circles, triangles, squares, arches, and squiggles. He also produces star shaped twinkles that are similarly colored.
|-|Cozy Pink=
Cozy Pink Blot is burgundy pink with darker shades for his makeup and feet. He also has three light freckles on his cheek, similar to the speckles on his legs. He wears a light pink bandana over his head with a white, scalloped pattern on the end of it. His shirt is also light pink and has mauve colored horizontal and vertical stripes, which are white where they intersect. The stitching on his gloves are also light pink.
|-|Sanguine Silence=
Sanguine Silence Blot is dark gray with blacker layers on his feet and similar layers on his hair. His eye appears with an angry expression and red makeup under it. He wears a black vampire cape with a red interior, a long, halved, cone-like collar, and four reverse-scallops at the edge. The cape also has seven evenly placed darker red stripes on the inside. He wears a crimson button shirt with two black buttons, and the sleeves are colored black.
|-|Chilly Penguin=
Chilly Penguin Blot is periwinkle with white face paint and a yellowish-orange cheek, while his legs turn into darker shades of periwinkle. He also dons a pair of earmuffs with a dark periwinkle headband and cups that are covered in white fluff. He wears a shirt with white fluff on the hem and collar and is as light as his shines with a dark periwinkle penguin design on it with a white, heart-shaped face, two dotted eyes colored black, and a yellowish-orange bill.
|-|Fancy Frosting=
Fancy Frosting Blot is pink with white face face paint, along with pastel purple makeup and pastel pink cheeks. His legs have lighter layers instead of darker, and his hair is now colored with similar lighter layers, leaving only the top of his head with a shine. His shirt has vertical stripes in pastel shades of pink, turquoise, yellow, and purple, and his sleeves are pastel yellow with white, scalloped cuffs. His gloves' stitching is also now pastel pink, and he wears white, puffy, scalloped shorts. He wears a standard bow tie colored pastel turquoise on his neck where ink would normally be situated, and also wears one on the right of his beret placed on the right side of his head. The beret has a white, petallike base and is light purple with a six-petaled, light yellow flower outline on the center with the inside being light pink and the button-shaped tail being light green.
|-|Inky Skull=
Inky Skull Blot is gray with legs and hair darkening to black, and the shine on the left side of his hair is longer like the top of his head, while the right side’s is arch-shaped. He now appears angry and has orange makeup around his eye, along with white face paint with three tooth-like markings on its lower half, resembling a skeleton skull. On his head, he sports a pair of dark gray headphones with orange ear pads and a black headband. He wears a black tee shirt with a white skull design on it, and his longer sleeves underneath are orange with black stripes, while the stitching on his gloves are colored black.
</tabber>

==Personality==
Despite what his looks might entail, Blot is actually quite a silly, funny, witty, and decently friendly mime-like [[Toon]] that is featured in the Circus Troupe, including his friends {{CI|Looey|name=true}} and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, as it is hinted by his walking and running animations, along with his dialogues. He's only capable of speaking backwards. He often uses this quirk of his to quip with the other Toons, whether it's to make fun of them without them knowing and making sarcastic remarks (even being seen talking in the third person when referring to Toons he's actively interacting with), or to simply toy with their understanding of what he's actually saying, showing his silly side. Sometimes this does backfire when said Toons shut down these quips by questioning him. Even so, he still shows a degree of concern and empathy towards Toons that he thinks are not doing well, and tries his best to cheer them up, as seen in his interactions with {{CI|Astro|name=true}} and {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}. As he is a mime, he seems to love {{wp|pantomiming}}, also shown while discussing act ideas with Looey and reacting with intrigue when {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} mentions performing arts literature.

Alongside his cheerful personality, he also seems to demonstrate a more mature and cynical side. He seems to thoroughly dislike extracting and runs in general, as shown in his "finishing extraction" lines, "descending to the next floor" lines, and some of his interactions. His dislike of extracting might reflect on his poor extraction stats. He appears to want to keep close tabs on his troupe, as hinted at by his interactions with {{CI|Vee|name=true}}, Looey, and Yatta, acting somewhat like the "parent" of the group. He seemingly has a bit of a love-hate relationship with Yatta in particular: sometimes he screams out demands at her when he's fed up with her carelessness, and other times he seems to find amusement in her antics.

Even though his troupe (mostly Yatta) seems to throw him around for a loop more often than not, he still seems to not want to replace his friends for the world, as proven in his interactions with Vee. This confirms that he deeply cares about his friends despite their setbacks.

The same cannot be said for Toons such as {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}, {{CI|Finn|name=true}}, and {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}. Their way of being and odd requests seem to tick him off to the point of tiring him out, showing his more cynical side.

Overall, Blot is a witty and sarcastic backwards-speaking Toon who occasionally finds enjoyment in making fun of others. He gets exhausted in regards to Toons whose antics he's not a fan of, but he's also mature enough to know when to drop the act when someone's not doing well, and to care for his close friends in the Circus Troupe.

