==Trivia==
*Blot is part of a Three [[Toon]] Circus Act known as the '''Circus Troupe''', with his role being that of a mime. The other two members are {{CI|Looey|name=true}} (a clown) and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} (an acrobat).
**Blot seems to be the calmest and most responsible member with helping Looey find his juggling pins, as seen in their interaction and Blot telling {{CI|Vee|name=true}} that Yatta and Looey need him.
*Blot was first officially mentioned in [[Changelog|v0.7.1]] during an interaction between [[Yatta]] and {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}.
**He's also briefly mentioned in an interaction between [[Looey]] and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}.
**Blot's earliest hint dates back to December 7, 2024, when [[Qwel]] reacted to someone asking about if the Circus Troupe includes a mime.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1314958870237675591</ref>
*Blot is [[Qwel]]'s favorite Circus Troupe [[Toon]] design.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1338250424926343289/1353052614870175827</ref>
*Blot is the third [[Toon]] to get released by himself, as well as the first male {{Type|Rare}} Toon.
*Blot is the third [[Toon]] to feature two different idle animations, with the first being [[Glisten]], and the second being {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}.
**[[Yatta]] and {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} could count, though their other animation is very consistent and possibly too fast for it to be counted as a separate idle/fidget.
*Blot leaves a trail of ink when he moves. He is currently the only [[Toon]] to have a trail in their default [[Skin]]. The trail itself is similar to the [[Ichor]] trails left by some {{Type|Main}} [[Twisteds]] and {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}}.
*Blot is the sixth non [[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to have a 5{{Star}} in a Stat, and the second with 5 Stars in Stamina specifically, with the first being {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} in the latter case.
*[[Blot Jr.]]'s eye drawing is also used as {{CI|Twisted Blot|name=true}}'s pupil.
*It is implied that Blot knows how to do shadow puppets since [[Twisted Blot]]'s hands resemble that of the shadow of a shadow dog puppet when scouting out players.
*Blot is the second [[Toon]] to wear gloves/hand coverings by default, with the first being {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}, and the third being [[Soulvester]].
*In the TV [[Show]], Blot does not speak as confirmed in one of {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]] dialogue. This likely meant Blot was able to teach himself or was taught how to speak (even if it was backwards) and explains why he knows sign language since that's how he would have communicated. At the same time, it could have been because they didn't want Blot to speak in the show due to the difficulty in understanding his reversed speech, and Blot might've always known how to speak.
**This makes him and {{CI|Flutter|name=true}} the only mute characters within the [[Show]].
*Blot is currently the second anthropomorphized [[Toon]] to talk differently compared to everyone else, the first being [[Flutter]].
**He is also the only Toon to talk backwards, and the reason why he talks this way is unknown.
**Unlike Flutter, not all Toons can understand Blot: the only ones that can are {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}, [[Looey]], [[Yatta]], [[Vee]], and [[Dazzle]]. The others have a harder time understanding him. However, he's still able to communicate with other Toons if he uses short and simple sentences so that the other Toons can understand Blot's words, as seen in {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}'s dialogue.
***[[Vee]] uses a built-in translator, and [[Dazzle]] can only understand him somewhat, not to the same degree as [[Yatta]] or [[Looey]]. Razzle, on the other hand, has no idea what he's saying. {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} and {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} also understand him sometimes, but he usually uses short phrases for talking. Gourdy seems to fully understand him like Yatta and Looey.
****Cosmo and Sprout's reason could also be their helpful personality making them want to learn how to understand him so they can cater to his needs.
***Blot would often use this gimmick as an excuse or an advantage to mock, tease, or make sarcastic remarks on other Toons without them knowing. Of course, this doesn't always work as he would expect, and that said Toons would usually shut down his comments by asking him what he was really saying.
*Blot does the art of pantomiming and general miming.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1375116135346737172</ref>
*Blot's [[Ability]] name, {{AI|Blot|name=true}}, was changed to '''Decoy''' for some reason shortly after his release. It was changed back the same day.
*Blot is the third Toon to have an ability that costs {{Tape|name=true}}, the previous two being [[Teagan]] and [[Sprout]].
**His Ability was the only one to not cost 100 Tapes prior to [[Changelog|v0.10.1]], as in that update Teagan's ability price went from 100 Tapes to 75. (Though, Blot still has the lowest tape price, unless there is 8 Blots.)
*Blot, {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, [[Cosmo]], and [[Bassie]] are the only Toons with 1{{Star}} Skill Check.
**Blot and Bassie are the second slowest extractors, with Shrimpo being the slowest.
**Blot was the last to release out of the four, with the first being Shrimpo, the second being Cosmo, and the third being Bassie.
*Blot is the third non-[[Main Character]] [[Toon]] that requires [[Mastery]] of another Toon (which are [[Looey]] and [[Yatta]]) to unlock them, with the first being {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, and the second being [[Looey]].
**He is the second non-Main Character to require *full* Mastery, after Looey.
**He is also currently the only Toon that requires 2 complete Masteries to be unlocked, needing full Mastery on Looey and Yatta.
*Blot, [[Scraps]], [[Sprout]], and {{CI|Bobette|name=true}} have 5 Stars on [[Stamina]].
*Blot is the third [[Toon]] to have a unique number of stars in each [[Stat]], with the first being [[Connie]], and the second being [[Yatta]].
**He is the only male to do so.
*Blot is currently the second most expensive non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] in the game, costing 3,000 [[Ichor]] to unlock.
**His total cost makes him the most expensive Toon; to unlock Blot, [[Looey]] and [[Yatta]] need finished [[Masteries]], with Yatta's requirements being to have at least 15 other Toons. This makes it cost a minimum of 18,000 Ichor to unlock him if one just started the game.
***If all the [[Event Toons]] (except the [[Mains]]) are included, the minimum Ichor required goes down to 7200 and 2500 of each Event [[Currency]].
*Blot has similar mechanics and gameplay to [[Sprout]] in terms of both their [[Abilities]] and [[Twisteds]]. 
**They share almost the same [[Stats]], with Blot having one less Star in [[Skill Check]].
**Their [[Abilities]] both require the use of [[Tapes]] and the cost increases when more of them are in the round.
***They also can save a [[Toon]].
**Their [[Twisted]] counterparts spawn black traps that damage [[Toons]] close to them.
***However, unlike {{CI|Twisted Sprout|name=true}}, [[Twisted Blot]] is stationary.
***Their [[Twisteds|Twisted counterparts]] also appear in the game's thumbnail.
*Blot's voting icon had his arms extend past his leg which have been shortened.
*Blot is the fourth [[Toon]] after {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, and {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} to only have one eye. This was proved in a storyboard artwork found in the [[Artist]] [[Floor]] featuring Blot, [[Looey]] and [[Yatta]], where Blot lifts his "hair" covering the left side of his face (right in our perspective), revealing no second eye, and in his interaction with Rodger. Why he has one eye is currently unknown.
**This also means that he is the second Toon to only have an eye for their face, after Rodger, and if counting, the {{TI|Whispering Flower|name=true}} [[Trinket]].
*Blot is the fourth Toon after [[Rodger]], [[Flutter]], and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} to not have visible mouths.
**{{CI|Soulvester|name=true}} could technically count, but the only reason is because of his helmet covering his face.
*Blot is the third [[Toon]] to have an [[Ability]] that loses LoS (Line of Sight) of [[Twisteds]], with the first being [[Connie]], second being [[Bobette]], and the fourth being [[Soulvester]].
**His is the only one to not affect Twisteds chasing him.
*Blot is quite different compared to the other Circus Troupe members.
**He doesn't have a predominant yellow color and any secondary colors, like [[Looey]]'s green and purple and [[Yatta]]'s blue and pink.
**He doesn't have a Passive [[Ability]].
**He doesn't have 2 Star Stealth.
**He is based off an ink blot, something not usually found in parties like Looey as a balloon or Yatta as a piñata.
**His [[Twisted Blot|Twisted counterpart]] isn't {{Type|Common}}.
**He doesn't have a fan made [[Skin]], like {{Skin|Dapperly Festive Looey}} and {{Skin|Choco Cones Yatta}}.
***Although {{Skin|Chilly Penguin Blot}} wasn't designed by [[Qwel]], the person who designed this skin is currently on the development team, which doesn't make this skin fanmade.
**His name is only 4 letters long and not 5, like Looey and Yatta.
***His name has no repeating/double letters unlike L'''oo'''ey and Ya'''tt'''a. He also has no Y in his name either.
**He has below average extraction, an antithesis to the other members's above average extraction.
**He has 2 idle fidgets.
**He does not have a custom damage effect.
**He has a special way of speaking unlike Looey and Yatta.
**His Ability doesn't directly interact with the [[Health]] system.
*If timed correctly, [[Blot Jr.]] can be placed in the elevator door, and when the door closes, it will still be there.
*Blot is one of the first non-[[Main Character]] [[Toons]] to get a [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]], with the other Toons being [[Looey]], [[Razzle & Dazzle]], and [[Yatta]].
**He is the first Toon to have a [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]] as one of their first Skins, being from the [[Show-Time Cosmetic Pack]].
*Blot is one of the first [[Toons]] to have both his normal counterpart and [[Twisted Blot|Twisted counterpart]] in a thumbnail, the other being [[Razzle & Dazzle]].
**Both Twisted Blot and Razzle & Dazzle are in the [[Changelog|v0.10]] banner.
*Blot has the highest permanent mobility compared to all of the non-[[Main Character]] [[Toons]] when ignoring [[Abilities]], having 9 Stars in [[Movement Speed]] and Stamina combined. However, Toons like [[Looey]] or [[Flutter]] can go much faster or further than Blot with the help of their Abilities.
**Therefore, Blot needs to travel the most meters for a non-Main Character for his [[Mastery]], with 120,000 meters.
*[[Blot Jr.]] does not work on long-ranged attacks from [[Twisteds]] such as {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}}. However, it will cause [[Twisted Sprout]] to summon a tendril at his location and {{CI|Twisted Bassie|name=true}} to shoot out vines towards him.
*Blot knows sign language according to a [[Minor Characters|kid]]'s drawing about him, where it talks about Blot using sign language with him, and when [[Gourdy]] asks Blot to teach him how to sign. This is reflective of real mimes who don't really talk, and use other forms of communication instead of speech such as gesticulation.
**It could also be the fact he never spoke in the [[show]], so other communication forms were needed and learned.
*His ink quality causes some trouble for him, like him leaving footprints around or staining things. Some even take advantage of this, with it being a running gag that all the artist characters ({{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}}, and [[Scraps]]) request for his help with their work, much to his annoyance.
*Blot wears 3 layers of gloves as his ink seeps through them easily, as confirmed in one of Blot's interactions with [[Razzle & Dazzle]].
*In a dialogue with [[Teagan]], Blot explains how he feels annoyed with [[Finn]] and [[Scraps]], but [[Teagan]] doesn't understand him correctly.
*Blot, along with [[Finn]], [[Gigi]], [[Yatta]], and [[Brusha]] are one of the only [[Toons]] to not have a full icon.
*Blot, along with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and [[Toodles]], is one of the only [[Toons]] to be predominantly grayscale.
**Unlike them, for his {{Skin|Vintage}} design, he was given a lighter color rather than a darker one.
*Blot seems to hate going on runs due to the fact that it involves extracting [[Machines]], which he finds boring and stressful. His minimal extraction [[Stats]] might be a factor to this.
*Along with [[Connie]], {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}, [[Ribecca]], and [[Flutter]], Blot is one of the 5 [[Toons]] to be immune to the {{Debuff|Illness|III}} and {{Debuff|Slow|I}} [[Debuffs]], as well as [[Ichor]] Stains from [[Ichor Puddles]]. 
*Blot is the first [[Toon]] capable of "stunning" [[Twisteds]], even if it is only one at a time and if from an [[Ability]] or, more specifically, their attack cooldown. The second to have this capability is [[Soulvester]] (with his adding extra time to the base attack cooldown).
*The sound Blot makes when he uses '''Blot Jr.''' is the same as the sound [[Yatta]] makes when '''Piñata Party''' is activated.
*Blot's {{Skin|Sanguine Silence}} [[Skin]] is the first and currently only Blot Skin to make a [[Blot Jr.]] with a different design, with Blot wearing a black cape while Blot Jr has bat wings and ears.
*In development, Blot's name could have been "Blott" (with two T's at the end), since multiple parts of the code refer to him as Blott, even after his release.
**In fact, a bit after his release, when a player attempted to purchase him without all requirements met (resulting in an unsuccessful purchase), an error appears saying "You do not meet the requirements for the Blott!".
***Additionally, when getting research from [[Twisted Blot]], the [[Capsule]] used to say "Twisted Blott".
*Blot is the last '''Non-Event''' {{Type|Rare}} to be in 2025.
*Blot reveals in dialogue with [[Gourdy]] that his mime performances are proficient enough for them to become a way of communicating with others. Gourdy himself is also practicing this talent, with Blot as his teacher. The Queens of Mischief music video also reveals he can use this talent of his as a dance move.

